Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] S2-10: GBA power-cut test (make -C gba test-cutsave),
 part of make -C gba test

A valid save of one island sits in slot 1; a save of another (the 58 KB worst case) is stopped K video frames
after it starts, with the harness keeping the flash file in sync as the ROM programs it, so the file is what a
power cut leaves. A fresh boot then reads the slot. Result on the flash design (trailer written last, the trailer
sector erased first, one copy per slot): K=100 (first encode pass, nothing written yet): the previous save is
intact and loads; K=350/450/560/650 (flash writes under way): the slot reads as empty, never torn; K=800
(finished): the new save verifies and loads with the right town. The rule is unchanged from before S2-10 (the
streamed save was already built this way); this makes it a test. On the GBA the previous save is only kept
through the first half of a save: there is one copy per slot.

